{
    "_comment": "Phase 1.6 A4 (100-clip × ~1000-step generalization). 100 train clips spanning 4 nuScenes scenes; 4 train_seen + 4 held_out_scene preview. Per §13.3 A4 + §13.10. Same FSDP bf16 stack as A2 v2 (now with optimizer-save fix in dwm_pano/distributed.py).",
    "_data": "100 train clips [0..99] (covers 4 nuScenes scenes per scripts/phase16_a4_scene_check.py). Held-out preview indices [106,142,174,206] each from a DIFFERENT scene, none overlapping train scenes (verified). PIN srun --nodelist=n3001-002 (only node with /local/data/val/rgb).",
    "_dtype_strategy": "fp32 base / bf16 FSDP compute / fp32 reduce / no grad_scaler. WHY: ctsd.py:866-868 does `model.to(dtype=self.model_dtype)` BEFORE FSDP wrap, so writing model_dtype=fp16 means FSDP's 'sharded params kept in full precision outside fwd/bwd' would actually be fp16 — not real fp32 master. Omit model_dtype → defaults to fp32 → FSDP master is real fp32. Then mixed_precision.param_dtype=bf16 (compute), reduce_dtype=fp32 (gradient allreduce precision), buffer_dtype=fp32. autocast also bf16 (default cuda autocast = fp16 — must match FSDP compute dtype). enable_grad_scaler=false (bf16 doesn't need it). Matches PyTorch FSDP2 tutorial canonical pattern.",
    "_preview_indices_note": "validation/preview pool [0,1,2,3, 106,142,174,206]: 4 train_seen + 4 held_out_scene, total 8 = WORLD_SIZE × batch_size to avoid DDP truncation (train.py:124-131). cycle: step100→clip0, 200→1, 300→2, 400→3, 500→106, 600→142, 700→174, 800→206, 900→0 (cycle restart), 1000→1. Each preview's clip + scene_token logged to preview/preview_debug.csv.",
    "_mesh_note": "mesh_shape=[4] (1D, single node × 4 GPUs). PyTorch FSDP1 docs: 'FULL_SHARD = 1D mesh; HYBRID_SHARD = 2D mesh'. Earlier [1,4] caused FSDP to take the OUTER dim (size 1) → world_size=1 → silent fallback to NO_SHARD → fp16 model + grad_scaler → NaN. Confirmed via PyTorch FSDP API doc (https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/fsdp.html).",
    "device": "cuda",
    "ddp_backend": "nccl",
    "_train_epochs_note": "100 clips / 4 ranks ≈ 25 batches/rank/epoch. train_epochs=40 → ~1000 batches/rank (effective batch=4 → 4000 sample-views). Init from df16 NOT from A2 v2's 750.pth (would carry 10-clip memorization bias).",
